+{
+  "number": 12,
+  "title": "Enforce structured schematized output for all agents via `aamf-json` fenced blocks",
+  "body": "## Summary\n\nAll agent definitions and the runtime should be amended so that agents **exclusively** communicate their results via structured, schematized output. Each agent must emit its final output as a fenced ` ```aamf-json ` code block containing a JSON payload conforming to an agent-specific schema. The runtime must parse this block, validate it against the schema, and mark the agent as **failed** if the output is missing, malformed, or non-conforming.\n\n## Motivation\n\nToday the runtime relies on a mix of strategies to interpret agent output:\n- **Exit codes** to determine success/failure (`AgentResult.success` is derived from `exitCode === 0`)\n- **Regex-based parsing** of stdout/stderr for token usage (`ResultParser.parseTokenUsage`)\n- **Regex-based markdown parsing** of migration plans (`ResultParser.parseMigrationPlanContent`)\n- **Optional sidecar `.result.json` files** (`ResultParser.readTaskResultJson`)\n- **File-system polling** for output file detection (`AgentLauncher.detectOutputFiles`)\n\nThis fragmented approach is fragile:\n1. **Agents can &#34;succeed&#34; (exit 0) without producing usable output** — the runtime has no way to verify the agent actually completed its task.\n2. **Markdown parsing is brittle** — the migration-planner agent already requires a very specific markdown format, and minor deviations silently drop tasks.\n3. **No uniform contract** — each agent has different output expectations, making it hard to add new agents or validate results consistently.\n4. **Token usage extraction is best-effort** — it scrapes stdout, which is unreliable.\n\nA single, mandatory structured output format solves all of these problems.\n\n## Proposed Design\n\n### 1. Agent-Side: `aamf-json` Output Block\n\nEvery agent definition (`.github/agents/*.agent.md`) must include explicit instructions requiring the agent to emit a fenced code block as its **final output**:\n\n````\n```aamf-json\n{\n  &#34;status&#34;: &#34;completed&#34; | &#34;failed&#34; | &#34;needs-review&#34;,\n  &#34;agent&#34;: &#34;&#34;,\n  &#34;taskId&#34;: &#34;&#34;,\n  ...agent-specific fields...\n}\n```\n````\n\nEach agent type defines its own schema extending a common base. Examples:\n\n#### Common Base Schema\n\n```typescript\nconst AamfOutputBase = z.object({\n  status: z.enum([&#39;completed&#39;, &#39;failed&#39;, &#39;needs-review&#39;]),\n  agent: z.string().min(1),\n  taskId: z.string().optional(),\n  tokenUsage: z.object({\n    prompt: z.number().int(),\n    completion: z.number().int(),\n    total: z.number().int(),\n  }).optional(),\n  notes: z.string().optional(),\n});\n```\n\n#### Agent-Specific Schemas (examples)\n\n**migration-planner**:\n```typescript\nconst MigrationPlannerOutput = AamfOutputBase.extend({\n  tasks: z.array(MigrationTaskSchema),  // replaces markdown parsing entirely\n  strategies: z.array(z.object({\n    name: z.string(),\n    rationale: z.string(),\n    selected: z.boolean(),\n  })),\n});\n```\n\n**code-migrator**:\n```typescript\nconst CodeMigratorOutput = AamfOutputBase.extend({\n  outputFiles: z.array(z.string()),\n  linesOfCode: z.number().int().optional(),\n  parity: z.enum([&#39;pass&#39;, &#39;partial&#39;, &#39;fail&#39;]).optional(),\n  issues: z.array(IssueSchema).default([]),\n});\n```\n\n**parity-verifier**:\n```typescript\nconst ParityVerifierOutput = AamfOutputBase.extend({\n  parityScore: z.number().min(0).max(1),\n  checks: z.array(z.object({\n    name: z.string(),\n    passed: z.boolean(),\n    details: z.string().optional(),\n  })),\n  issues: z.array(IssueSchema).default([]),\n});\n```\n\n### 2. Runtime-Side: Parsing &amp; Validation\n\n#### `ResultParser` changes\n\nAdd a new method to extract and validate the `aamf-json` block from agent stdout:\n\n```typescript\nstatic parseAamfOutput(\n  stdout: string,\n  schema: T,\n): z.infer | { error: string }\n```\n\nLogic:\n1. Scan stdout for the **last** fenced block tagged `aamf-json`\n2. Extract the JSON content\n3. Validate against the provided Zod schema\n4. Return the parsed object or an error description\n\n#### `AgentLauncher` changes\n\nAfter capturing stdout, the launcher should:\n1. Call `ResultParser.parseAamfOutput(stdout, agentSchema)` with the schema for the invoked agent\n2. If parsing fails → set `AgentResult.success = false` and populate `AgentResult.error` with the parse failure reason, **regardless of exit code**\n3. Attach the parsed structured data to `AgentResult` (new field: `structuredOutput?: Record`)\n\n#### `Orchestrator` changes\n\nPhase handlers should consume `AgentResult.structuredOutput` directly instead of doing ad-hoc file reads or markdown parsing. For example:\n- Phase 3 (planning): read `tasks` from the planner&#39;s structured output instead of parsing `migration-plan.md`\n- Phase 4 (migration): read `outputFiles` and `parity` from the migrator&#39;s structured output\n- Phase 5 (verification): read `parityScore` and `issues` from the verifier&#39;s structured output\n\n### 3. Agent Definition Updates\n\nAll 14 agent definitions need to be updated:\n\n| Agent | Key output fields in `aamf-json` |\n|---|---|\n| `migration-orchestrator` | `phases`, `overallStatus` |\n| `impact-assessor` | `riskLevel`, `impactedModules`, `complexityBreakdown` |\n| `knowledge-builder` | `modules`, `indexPath` |\n| `large-file-analyzer` | `chunks`, `fileAnalysis` |\n| `migration-planner` | `tasks`, `strategies` |\n| `adjudicator` | `selectedStrategy`, `rationale`, `modifications` |\n| `code-migrator` | `outputFiles`, `linesOfCode`, `parity`, `issues` |\n| `parity-verifier` | `parityScore`, `checks`, `issues` |\n| `test-writer` | `testFiles`, `testCount`, `coverage` |\n| `failure-recovery` | `diagnosis`, `fixApplied`, `fixFiles` |\n| `final-parity-checker` | `overallParity`, `fixes` |\n| `e2e-test-crafter` | `testFiles`, `scenarios` |\n| `documentation-writer` | `docFiles`, `sections` |\n| `migration-runner` | `buildStatus`, `testStatus`, `commands` |\n\nEach agent prompt must include:\n1. The exact JSON schema it must conform to (inline in the prompt)\n2. A `## Output Format` section explaining the `aamf-json` block requirement\n3. An example of a valid output block\n4. A warning that the runtime will reject non-conforming output\n\n### 4. `AgentResult` Type Extension\n\n```typescript\nexport interface AgentResult {\n  // ...existing fields...\n  \n  /** Parsed structured output from the agent&#39;s aamf-json block. */\n  structuredOutput?: Record;\n  \n  /** Whether the aamf-json block was successfully parsed. */\n  outputParsed: boolean;\n  \n  /** Parse error if the aamf-json block was missing or invalid. */\n  parseError?: string;\n}\n```\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n### Runtime (`runtime/src/`)\n- `agents/types.ts` — Add `structuredOutput`, `outputParsed`, `parseError` to `AgentResult`; add per-agent Zod schemas\n- `agents/result-parser.ts` — Add `parseAamfOutput()` method; define agent schema registry\n- `core/agent-launcher.ts` — Integrate `parseAamfOutput` into post-execution flow; fail agents with bad output\n- `core/orchestrator.ts` — Refactor phase handlers to use `structuredOutput` instead of ad-hoc parsing\n\n### Agent Definitions (`.github/agents/`)\n- All 14 `*.agent.md` files — Add `## Output Format` section with schema, example, and enforcement warning\n\n### Tests (`runtime/tests/`)\n- `result-parser.test.ts` — Tests for `parseAamfOutput` with valid/invalid/missing blocks\n- New: `aamf-output-schema.test.ts` — Schema validation tests for each agent type\n- Update existing orchestrator/e2e tests to expect structured output\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every agent definition includes an `## Output Format` section with `aamf-json` block instructions\n- [ ] `ResultParser.parseAamfOutput()` correctly extracts and validates `aamf-json` blocks from stdout\n- [ ] Agents that exit 0 but produce invalid/missing `aamf-json` output are marked as **failed** by the runtime\n- [ ] Token usage is extracted from the structured output (not scraped from stdout)\n- [ ] Migration plan tasks are parsed from structured JSON (not regex-based markdown parsing)\n- [ ] All existing tests pass with the new structured output flow\n- [ ] Backward compatibility: the runtime gracefully handles agents that haven&#39;t been updated yet (log warning, fall back to legacy parsing) during the transition period",
+  "labels": [
+    "",
+    "",
+    ""
+  ],
+  "assignees": [],
+  "comments": [],
+  "state": "open",
+  "createdAt": "",
+  "updatedAt": "",
+  "linkedPRs": []
+}
